# --- BeastPing Mail Console: message archive (MAIL-CONTENT-01) ---------------
# PROPOSAL FOR REVIEW. Not applied by any Mail Console script.
#
# 1) A second cleanup service, identical to the standard one except that it
#    adds one hidden envelope recipient to every message it handles. Postfix
#    adds always_bcc recipients with NOTIFY=NONE: an archive problem never
#    produces a bounce or delay notice to the sender. Copy the private/chroot
#    columns from your existing "cleanup" line (Ubuntu default shown).
cleanup-archive unix  n       -       y       -       0       cleanup
  -o always_bcc=archive@mail-console.invalid

# 2) Delivery of that archive copy to the capture program (standard library
#    Python, runs as the unprivileged user mcarchive, writes only into
#    /var/spool/mail-console/incoming, never contacts the console or network).
#    At most 4 captures run at once.
mailconsole-archive unix -    n       n       -       4       pipe
  user=mcarchive argv=/usr/local/libexec/mail-console/mc-capture --queue-id=${queue_id} --sender=${sender} --sasl-user=${sasl_username}

# 3) On the EXISTING public authenticated submission listener add ONE option.
#    On the BeastPing server that listener is named 91.107.182.219:submission
#    (the loopback 127.0.0.1:submission listener is not captured):
#
#    91.107.182.219:submission inet n - y - - smtpd
#      ...existing -o options unchanged...
#      -o cleanup_service_name=cleanup-archive
#
#    Use deploy/capture_postfix.py (plan/apply/deactivate) rather than editing
#    by hand: it discovers the listener, mirrors the cleanup columns, keeps
#    transport_maps, verifies routing and restores the exact previous values.
